{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "tc_dot: a block FMA of 8 f16 products and an f32 c (Ampere's f16 HMMA with f32 accumulate, as modelled by arXiv 2512.07004)\n  semantics: products exact; aligned to E, the largest exponent among the products and c (at least -132), in a window of 24 fractional bits, each term truncated toward zero; one exact integer sum; normalised once and truncated to f32\n  bound (derived): |tc_dot - sum T| < 9 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S| <= 9 2^-24 max|T| + 2^-23 |sum T| + ..., T the 9 products and c, S the window's sum\n    each term loses less than one unit of the window, 2^(E-24), by its truncation (none for a term on the window's grid); the final truncation to 24 bits loses less than 2^-23 |S|; and 2^E <= max|T| where the largest term's significand is at least 1 (normal inputs)\n    relative to the largest term, not to sum |T|: with cancellation the result's own relative error is unbounded\n  checked on 256 random blocks (sampled, seed 1): the operation as written and an independent transcription agree on 256; the bound holds on 256, the error at most 0.533 of it\n  largest error relative to max|T|: 2.48e-07 (2^-24 = 5.96e-08); relative to |sum T|: 1.13e-06\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "tcdot", "ucas": "tcdot", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tcdot", "terms": 9, "bound": "(n+1) 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S|", "max_error_over_max_term": 2.483764536595241e-07, "max_error_over_sum": 1.131297794851255e-06}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sampled", "points": 256, "max_diff": 0.5330021798180373, "passed": true, "text": "the bound on random blocks, and the operation against an independent transcription"}], "files": [], "text": "tc_dot: a block FMA of 8 f16 products and an f32 c (Ampere's f16 HMMA with f32 accumulate, as modelled by arXiv 2512.07004)\n  semantics: products exact; aligned to E, the largest exponent among the products and c (at least -132), in a window of 24 fractional bits, each term truncated toward zero; one exact integer sum; normalised once and truncated to f32\n  bound (derived): |tc_dot - sum T| < 9 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S| <= 9 2^-24 max|T| + 2^-23 |sum T| + ..., T the 9 products and c, S the window's sum\n    each term loses less than one unit of the window, 2^(E-24), by its truncation (none for a term on the window's grid); the final truncation to 24 bits loses less than 2^-23 |S|; and 2^E <= max|T| where the largest term's significand is at least 1 (normal inputs)\n    relative to the largest term, not to sum |T|: with cancellation the result's own relative error is unbounded\n  checked on 256 random blocks (sampled, seed 1): the operation as written and an independent transcription agree on 256; the bound holds on 256, the error at most 0.533 of it\n  largest error relative to max|T|: 2.48e-07 (2^-24 = 5.96e-08); relative to |sum T|: 1.13e-06\n"}, "isError": false}}
